    "['mpls', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'mpls ip', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nmpls ip\\n##\\n\\nExplanation: In Cisco IOS, `mpls ip` is the equivalent command to Huawei's `mpls` command for enabling MPLS on an interface. While Huawei uses a simple `mpls` command, Cisco requires the `mpls ip` form to enable MPLS processing on an interface.\", 'trans_template': 'mpls ip'}]]": 1,
    "['mpls te', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'mpls traffic-eng', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nmpls traffic-eng\\n##\\n\\nExplanation: The Huawei `mpls te` command enables MPLS Traffic Engineering (TE) globally on the device. The equivalent Cisco IOS command is `mpls traffic-eng`. Both commands serve the same purpose of enabling MPLS traffic engineering capabilities on the router.', 'trans_template': 'mpls traffic-eng'}]]": 1,
    "['mpls te bandwidth max-reservable-bandwidth [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'interface GigabitEthernet2/0/0', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent command for Huawei's `mpls te bandwidth max-reservable-bandwidth 20000`:\\n\\n##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet2/0/0\\n mpls traffic-eng bandwidth 20000\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Cisco IOS, this command sets both the maximum reservable bandwidth and the global pool bandwidth (BC0) simultaneously, unlike Huawei where they are configured separately. The value (20000) should be in kbps for both platforms.\", 'trans_template': 'interface GigabitEthernet2/0/0'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'mpls traffic-eng bandwidth 20000', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent command for Huawei's `mpls te bandwidth max-reservable-bandwidth 20000`:\\n\\n##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet2/0/0\\n mpls traffic-eng bandwidth 20000\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Cisco IOS, this command sets both the maximum reservable bandwidth and the global pool bandwidth (BC0) simultaneously, unlike Huawei where they are configured separately. The value (20000) should be in kbps for both platforms.\", 'trans_template': 'mpls traffic-eng bandwidth 20000'}]]": 1,
    "['mpls te bandwidth [parameter1] [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'mpls traffic-eng bandwidth 20000', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the equivalent Cisco command for the HUAWEI `mpls te bandwidth bc0 20000` configuration:\\n\\n##\\nmpls traffic-eng bandwidth 20000\\n##\\n\\nThis Cisco command configures the maximum reservable bandwidth for MPLS TE on an interface, which is the equivalent functionality to Huawei's BC0 bandwidth class configuration. The value 20000 represents the bandwidth in kbps.\", 'trans_template': 'mpls traffic-eng bandwidth 20000'}]]": 1,
    "['mpls rsvp-te', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'mpls traffic-eng tunnels', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the equivalent Cisco command for `mpls rsvp-te`:\\n\\n##\\nmpls traffic-eng tunnels\\nip rsvp bandwidth\\n##\\n\\nThe Cisco equivalent requires both commands to enable RSVP-TE functionality:\\n1. `mpls traffic-eng tunnels` enables MPLS TE features\\n2. `ip rsvp bandwidth` enables RSVP for bandwidth reservation (defaults to 75% of interface bandwidth if no value specified)\", 'trans_template': 'mpls traffic-eng tunnels'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ip rsvp bandwidth', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the equivalent Cisco command for `mpls rsvp-te`:\\n\\n##\\nmpls traffic-eng tunnels\\nip rsvp bandwidth\\n##\\n\\nThe Cisco equivalent requires both commands to enable RSVP-TE functionality:\\n1. `mpls traffic-eng tunnels` enables MPLS TE features\\n2. `ip rsvp bandwidth` enables RSVP for bandwidth reservation (defaults to 75% of interface bandwidth if no value specified)\", 'trans_template': 'ip rsvp bandwidth'}]]": 1,
